# SignCOMPASS

**COMPASS: Complementary Motion and Appearance Streams for Isolated Sign Recognition**

Anonymized code release for peer review. Two-stream isolated sign language recognition: a pose stream (MediaPipe keypoints -> Conformer) captures motion, an appearance stream (MediaPipe face/hand crops -> DINOv2 -> fine-tuned SHuBERT) captures shape, and a simple score fusion combines them.

| Dataset (language)   | Pose | SHuBERT | Fusion |
|----------------------|:----:|:-------:|:------:|
| ASL-Citizen (ASL)    | 64.3 | 64.3    | 71.0   |
| WLASL-2000 (ASL)*    | 22.1 | 24.4    | 27.5   |
| AUTSL (Turkish)      | 92.3 | 91.7    | 93.7   |
| INCLUDE (Indian)     | 97.5 | 97.0    | 96.7   |

*57% class-coverage subset (relative comparison only).

## Quickstart

    conda create -n compass python=3.10 -y && conda activate compass
    pip install -r requirements.txt

## Train and evaluate (each script takes --dataset: asl_citizen, wlasl, autsl, include)

    python extract_pose_islr.py        --dataset asl_citizen
    python extract_shubert_features.py --dataset asl_citizen
    python train_islr.py               --dataset asl_citizen
    python train_shubert_ft.py         --dataset asl_citizen
    python multi_ensemble.py           --dataset asl_citizen --alpha 0.5

Fusion rule: P(y|V) = (1 - alpha) * p_pose + alpha * p_shubert, alpha tuned on validation (best alpha = 0.5 on ASL-Citizen).

## Method

Each stream ends in an ArcFace head over 2,731 signs. Pose: 4-layer Conformer on 261-d MediaPipe Holistic keypoints. Appearance: MediaPipe face/hand crops through a frozen DINOv2 ViT-S/14 and a fine-tuned 12-layer SHuBERT transformer. Scores are averaged with one tuned weight.

